<Layout id="cache" title="Caching">

  <h1>Memory Higharchy</h1>

    <img
    src="/images/cache.png"
    class="figure"
  />

  <p>
    In the TM5400, the cache hierarchy consists of a separate L1 instruction
    cache, L1 data cache, and a larger L2 write back cache.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>L1 Instruction Cache: Stores recently fetched molecules.</li>
    <li>L1 Data Cache: Stores data loaded and stored by code.</li>
    <li>L2 Cache: Larger writeback cache between the L1 caches and DRAM.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Generated translations are stored in a reserved region of normal DRAM called
    the Translation Cache. This is separate from the hardware L1 and L2 caches.
  </p>

  <p>
    Stores also pass through a gated store buffer before entering
    the normal memory system. More about this in the Precise Exceptions page.
  </p>

</Layout>